# SEO

Treat Google discoverability as an architectural requirement.

For public pages:
- semantic URLs;
- unique title;
- unique meta description;
- canonical where appropriate;
- Open Graph metadata;
- sitemap;
- robots;
- structured data when justified;
- semantic HTML;
- crawlable primary content;
- optimized images and meaningful alt text;
- good performance/Core Web Vitals;
- no accidental duplicate pages.

Private application routes must not be indexed.

Do not expose student/teacher private data through public metadata.

# Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA.

Required:
- keyboard navigation;
- visible focus;
- semantic buttons/links;
- associated form labels;
- accessible validation/error messages;
- sufficient contrast;
- do not communicate meaning by color alone;
- heading hierarchy;
- landmarks;
- accessible tables;
- screen-reader-friendly state changes;
- sensible touch targets;
- `prefers-reduced-motion`;
- avoid unnecessary ARIA;
- dialogs/modals must manage focus correctly.

Every new UI feature must be checked for keyboard, focus, contrast, labels and error states.

# UX

Minimalist, professional, adult education experience.

Use existing Omegon visual tokens/components first.
If the project has no established palette, centralize the new palette as tokens rather than hardcoding colors across components.

Do not make the interface look like a children's gamification app.
